11:55.376 --> 11:56.912
Uh, Stewie?

11:58.531 --> 12:00.134
Oh, crap.

12:00.168 --> 12:03.856
This is not the way out!
This is not the way out!

12:07.230 --> 12:09.600
Hey, Horace, get that
wiener out of your hand

12:09.635 --> 12:11.636
and give us three more beers
over here!

12:11.670 --> 12:14.340
(laughs) Lois, you're always
giving me the business.

12:14.375 --> 12:16.194
(laughter)

12:16.229 --> 12:18.415
Hey, I meant
to tell you guys.

12:18.449 --> 12:20.252
We shot some drug dealer
this morning,

12:20.287 --> 12:22.824
and he had three Red Sox
tickets in his pocket.

12:22.858 --> 12:23.825
That's awesome!

12:23.859 --> 12:25.762
Oh, this'll be so fun!

12:25.796 --> 12:27.481
You know, if we leave
right now,

12:27.516 --> 12:30.069
we can probably still get there
before the first pitch.

12:30.103 --> 12:31.205
Hey, you guys.

12:31.239 --> 12:32.974
Oh, hey, Peter.
How's it going?

12:33.008 --> 12:35.145
Peter, it's so good
to see you up and around!

12:35.179 --> 12:36.813
Yeah, how ya feeling?

12:36.848 --> 12:38.033
I'm feeling shipshape.

12:38.067 --> 12:39.969
<i>If the ship is
the S.S. Minnow!</i>

12:40.004 --> 12:41.739
Doctor said I'd be
making bland jokes

12:41.773 --> 12:44.110
for about a week,
then I'd be good as new.

12:44.144 --> 12:45.312
Ah, that's good to hear.

12:45.346 --> 12:47.783
Well, we were just on
our way up to Fenway.

12:47.817 --> 12:49.151
Aw, you got tickets?
That's sweet.

12:49.185 --> 12:50.621
You know, there's
no better outing

12:50.656 --> 12:52.791
than watching
nine innings.

12:52.825 --> 12:53.861
(coughs)

12:53.895 --> 12:55.463
Sorry, I'll perk up
at the game.

12:55.498 --> 12:58.035
Oh, well, actually,
we only have three tickets,

12:58.069 --> 12:59.437
and we're going with Lois.

12:59.471 --> 13:00.773
With Lois?

13:00.807 --> 13:02.075
Oh, yeah, we've actually been

13:02.109 --> 13:03.444
having a great time with her.

13:03.478 --> 13:04.947
And she's quite
a bowler, too.

13:04.981 --> 13:06.149
Is that all right,
Peter?

13:06.183 --> 13:08.953
Do you mind if I go
to the game with the guys?

13:08.987 --> 13:10.088
Yeah, no, that's,
that's fine.

13:10.122 --> 13:12.125
I mean, yeah, you only
got three tickets.

13:12.160 --> 13:13.660
I mean, that's cool.
Have fun.

13:13.695 --> 13:15.397
Okay, we'll see you later.

13:17.234 --> 13:18.803
(sighs) Hey, Horace,

13:18.837 --> 13:20.923
why don't you take that
wiener out of your hand

13:20.957 --> 13:22.092
and get me a beer.

13:22.127 --> 13:24.580
Don't talk to me that way,
you son of a bitch!

13:32.312 --> 13:33.279
Oh, hey, Peter!

13:33.313 --> 13:34.314
Oh, hey.

13:34.348 --> 13:35.983
Did you have fun
at the game?

13:36.018 --> 13:37.520
Oh, yeah,
it was so exciting.

13:37.554 --> 13:39.857
They scored the winning hit
right at the buzzer.

13:39.892 --> 13:41.126
I'm sorry you missed it.

13:41.160 --> 13:42.662
Yeah, no,
th-that's okay.

13:42.696 --> 13:45.500
I've just been hanging out here
having a great time with...

13:45.534 --> 13:46.769
Meg?!
Hey.

13:46.803 --> 13:49.205
I thought you was a bag
of peeling potatoes.

13:49.240 --> 13:50.709
Well, maybe next time
you can come

13:50.743 --> 13:52.746
with us when we go
to Red Sock Field.

13:52.781 --> 13:54.348
Nobody calls it that.

13:54.382 --> 13:57.554
Quags and Swanny were so funny
yelling things at the visitors.

13:57.588 --> 13:58.655
Quags and Swanny?!

13:58.691 --> 14:00.459
Lois, it's one thing
to steal my friends,

14:00.493 --> 14:02.480
but don't go giving them
stupid new nicknames.

14:02.514 --> 14:03.798
What are you
talking about?

14:03.832 --> 14:05.402
I didn't steal
your friends, Peter.

14:05.437 --> 14:07.706
I'm only doing
what you asked me to do.

14:07.740 --> 14:09.810
No, I asked you
to take my place

14:09.844 --> 14:11.713
at the bowling
tournament, that's it!

14:11.747 --> 14:13.148
Look, Lois, I have
my friends,

14:13.183 --> 14:14.417
and you have groceries

14:14.452 --> 14:16.420
and all those rusty
pink razors in the shower.

14:16.455 --> 14:18.391
Now just stick to what's
intended for you

14:18.425 --> 14:19.727
and leave my
things to me.

14:19.761 --> 14:21.196
Are you saying
you want me

14:21.230 --> 14:23.199
to stop hanging out
with Joe and Quagmire?

14:23.233 --> 14:24.936
<i>They're my friends.
They're all I got!</i>

14:24.970 --> 14:26.704
And you know
how hard it is

14:26.739 --> 14:28.208
for me to make
new friends.

14:33.935 --> 14:36.355
Is this friends?

14:41.215 --> 14:42.651
Stewie, we're never
gonna find him.

14:42.685 --> 14:44.152
They're all
exactly the same.

14:44.187 --> 14:47.525
Wow. I wish you could hear how
racist you sound right now.

14:47.560 --> 14:48.828
Come on. Can't you give

14:48.862 --> 14:50.497
that giraffe at home
another chance?

14:50.531 --> 14:52.199
You know, for every one
they sell,

14:52.234 --> 14:53.968
they save a giraffe
in the wild.

14:54.002 --> 14:55.989
(gunfire)

14:56.023 --> 14:59.829
MAN: Sorry, giraffes!
They only bought one!

14:59.863 --> 15:02.317
Nah, they returned it!

15:06.140 --> 15:07.976
And so Lois sweet-talks
her way backstage.

15:08.011 --> 15:09.344
Next thing you know,

15:09.379 --> 15:11.248
we're partying all night
with the trapeze people!

15:11.283 --> 15:13.085
One of them drives a Volvo!

15:13.119 --> 15:15.656
<i>Drives a super-safe car,
does that for a living!</i>

15:15.690 --> 15:16.690
Go figure!

15:16.724 --> 15:18.545
(laughing)

15:18.579 --> 15:20.933
So what? She can name
a kind of car.

15:20.967 --> 15:22.769
Big whoop.
I can do that, too.

15:22.803 --> 15:23.871
Vikki.

15:23.905 --> 15:25.140
Vikki Carr.

15:25.174 --> 15:26.809
Peter, relax.
It just happens

15:26.844 --> 15:29.012
that your wife has some
funny stories, that's all.

15:29.047 --> 15:31.417
Well, I got some
funny stories.

15:31.451 --> 15:33.688
I knew a guy
who choked on an almond.

15:33.722 --> 15:35.023
And he had a stroke.

15:35.058 --> 15:37.361
Now he can't take care
of his own bathroom needs.

15:37.395 --> 15:38.796
(laughs)

15:38.830 --> 15:40.483
That's not funny.
That sounds sad.

15:40.517 --> 15:42.019
Yeah, I feel
bad for him.

15:42.053 --> 15:43.488
Oh, don't feel bad
for him.

15:43.522 --> 15:45.090
He got his name
in the paper.

15:45.125 --> 15:47.378
What?
(laughs)

15:47.412 --> 15:49.014
(sobbing):
Please look at me!

15:49.048 --> 15:50.650
What the hell's wrong
with you, Peter?

15:50.684 --> 15:52.567
Nothing. What the hell's
wrong with you, Swanny?

15:52.589 --> 15:53.890
I'm Quags.

15:53.924 --> 15:56.828
(sobbing): I don't know
who any of you are anymore!

15:56.862 --> 15:58.532
Oh, he's really upset.

15:58.566 --> 16:00.201
I haven't seen him like this

16:00.235 --> 16:02.237
since he saw
that Rocky Dennis movie.

16:02.272 --> 16:05.827
Take off the mask!
That's your problem!

16:05.862 --> 16:07.063
Right?

16:11.238 --> 16:13.624
That's it, Brian.
He's not here.

16:13.659 --> 16:15.527
None of these
bears are Rupert.

16:15.562 --> 16:16.863
Stewie...

16:16.897 --> 16:19.801
(sighs) You don't have
to say it, Brian. I know.

16:21.088 --> 16:24.259
So this is what it feels
like to be a grown-up, huh?

16:24.293 --> 16:26.329
All alone in the world.

16:26.364 --> 16:29.536
Look, Stewie,
nothing lasts forever.

16:29.570 --> 16:31.939
You and Rupert had
some special times together,

16:31.973 --> 16:33.476
and you'll always have that.

16:33.510 --> 16:34.677
(clanking)

16:34.711 --> 16:36.179
What the deuce?
What's that noise?

16:36.214 --> 16:37.214
I don't know.

16:46.948 --> 16:49.268
Oh, my God!
Brian, look!

16:52.542 --> 16:53.692
That's him!
That's Rupert!

16:53.727 --> 16:55.162
How do you know?

16:55.197 --> 16:56.797
You can't hear
him calling me?

16:56.832 --> 16:58.268
He's calling me,
clear as day!

16:58.302 --> 17:00.070
Ah. Yeah,
now I hear him.

17:00.105 --> 17:02.474
Rupert, yes, we're here
to rescue you!

17:02.509 --> 17:03.827
Stewie, wait!
It's too dangerous!

17:03.861 --> 17:06.031
I won't let it end
like this, Brian!

17:20.891 --> 17:22.844
Don't you give up on me, Rupert!

17:22.895 --> 17:24.563
Hang on, Stewie!
Maybe I can help!

17:24.597 --> 17:25.966
Maybe I can use this helicopter

17:25.984 --> 17:27.686
to knock Rupert off
the conveyor belt...

17:27.737 --> 17:29.138
Ah! Son of a bitch!

17:29.172 --> 17:30.857
Recall room, Brian.
Nothing works in here.

17:30.908 --> 17:32.527
Now come on!
Rupert's in trouble!

17:32.579 --> 17:34.530
Okay, I'm coming, I'm coming.

17:34.581 --> 17:36.984
(barking)

17:42.212 --> 17:44.432
Almost there.
You can do this, Stewie.

18:02.529 --> 18:04.750
♪

18:23.950 --> 18:25.153
(toy squeaks)

18:25.187 --> 18:25.920
Damn it!

18:25.954 --> 18:28.925
Brian, do something!

18:36.806 --> 18:38.141
(gears grinding)

18:46.205 --> 18:47.908
(sighs)

18:47.942 --> 18:51.163
Oh, Rupert!
Thank God, you're alive!

18:51.214 --> 18:53.385
I'm... I'm ready now.

18:53.419 --> 18:55.388
I'm ready to get off the pill.

18:55.422 --> 18:58.459
I think we should start trying.

19:02.050 --> 19:03.953
Look, Peter, I think
there's something

19:03.987 --> 19:05.522
we should talk about.

19:05.557 --> 19:07.926
I'm not reading the last page
of that dinosaur book.

19:07.961 --> 19:09.796
I know something bad
happens to 'em.

19:09.830 --> 19:11.398
No, Peter, we need
to talk about

19:11.433 --> 19:12.802
this situation
with the guys.

19:12.836 --> 19:16.324
Look, of course I like hanging
out with Joe and Quagmire.

19:16.342 --> 19:19.162
But I like hanging out
with you more.

19:19.180 --> 19:22.467
I mean, it's nice to make
new friends, but not if it means

19:22.501 --> 19:24.805
losing the best friend
I've ever had.

19:24.839 --> 19:27.125
Yeah, well, I was
probably kind of a jerk, too.

19:27.159 --> 19:29.364
I guess I shouldn't be
telling you who you can

19:29.398 --> 19:30.867
and can't be
friends with.

19:30.902 --> 19:32.002
(knocking)

19:32.804 --> 19:34.039
Hey, you guys want to go

19:34.073 --> 19:35.892
with me and Joe
to the roller derby?

19:35.926 --> 19:37.863
It's great. You get
to see big, husky chicks

19:37.897 --> 19:39.614
elbow each other
right in the jugs.

19:39.649 --> 19:40.918
Oh, that sounds like fun.

19:40.952 --> 19:42.185
Yeah, and I'm bringing
my grill

19:42.220 --> 19:44.974
so we can eat corn in the
parking lot before we go in.

19:45.008 --> 19:46.192
What do you say?
Who's in?

19:46.227 --> 19:47.194
Sounds great!

19:47.229 --> 19:49.114
Yeah, that'll be really...

19:51.987 --> 19:53.322
You know what, you guys?

19:53.357 --> 19:55.693
I think I'm gonna
just stay in tonight.

19:55.728 --> 19:58.330
I got a huge stack
of coupons to go through.

19:58.365 --> 20:00.534
Plus, I'm planning on having
my period really hard later,

20:00.569 --> 20:03.240
and I want to be
in the tub when it happens.

20:03.275 --> 20:05.109
You what?!
Gross.

20:05.143 --> 20:06.461
Oh, I get it.

20:06.495 --> 20:08.332
Guys, I think Lois
is getting a visit

20:08.366 --> 20:09.600
from her Aunt Period.

20:09.634 --> 20:11.337
Yeah, and lots
of other chick stuff

20:11.371 --> 20:13.556
you guys wouldn't be
interested in.

20:13.590 --> 20:17.045
Peter, go have fun
with your friends.

20:17.080 --> 20:19.116
Thanks, Lois.

20:22.489 --> 20:25.494
Oh, hey, Brian.
Where have you been?

20:25.528 --> 20:27.230
Oh, just reuniting
some old friends.

20:27.264 --> 20:28.549
Huh. Me, too.

20:28.583 --> 20:30.285
Feels good, doesn't it?

20:30.320 --> 20:31.988
Sure does.

20:33.359 --> 20:34.693
I love you, Rupert.

20:34.727 --> 20:36.697
Don't you ever leave me again.

20:36.731 --> 20:40.136
(sighs, choking)

20:46.182 --> 20:48.952
Mom, Stewie's dead!

20:53.828 --> 20:55.262
[ sirens blaring ]

20:55.264 --> 20:56.698
[ buzzer sounds ]

20:56.700 --> 20:58.619
[ gasps ]

20:58.620 --> 21:59.620
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru